LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Mix"
English mix in management accounting means the proportions in which things are sold or used, and it appears in three compounds the exam uses without explanation: sales mix, the proportions of products sold; product mix, often the same thing and sometimes the range offered; and mix variance, the part of a profit difference caused by proportions rather than by volume or price. Arabic مزيج covers all three. French uses mix as a borrowing in mix des ventes and mix produits, and composition for the general sense — and note that French mixte means mixed in the sense of combined, as in coût mixte, a semi-variable cost, which is an entirely different idea from mix. Read the compound, not the word.
